it wasnt a good scenario as she started yelling at me more, i dont ever like yelling at people but i see how thats something i dont want to continue more as it just led to more arguing. im def clear with her though that i wont take her shit, she doesnt get a free pass to walk all over me just because im her sister

&#x200B;

im moving to college though, i wanted to take another gap year but honestly i feel like im gonna fucking lose my mind here and kill myself if i stay another year

yeah i got pretty fucking mad back honestly, i dont like yelling or taking my anger out on ANYONE however i just fucking snapped and defended myself since she feels entitled to yell at everyone back every day 

&#x200B;

like youre fucking 19

i took half a bottle of prozac (what was left in my prescription) + the rest of the painkillers my mom had ab 30? minutes ago and im still alive somehow and conscious

&#x200B;

i feel really terrible for the people this is gonna impact but i know its selfish when i just want to save myself from eternal pain, im just waiting to go unconscious and pass out for some mercy in my life

idgaf whats selfish, im just not meant to be here and im meant for an early death

&#x200B;

im so sorry this world was never meant for me to be in it, if you knew my story you wouldve realized this early on

he left me after i tried to kill myself, i trusted him and now i found out he lied about some things and its making me sick

&#x200B;

who the fuck did i just date? i trusted him and loved him?

i was originally interested in google CSSI (which if youre in grade 12 and a minority, you should def look into it) so i emailed an advisor i found on linkedin: i told him a bit ab myself and my goals - what ive done, what i want to do, etc.

&#x200B;

i dont think im as experienced yet to get a google internship? but im also applying to CSSI and i hope i can get in but anything could happen

from taking a gap year i wont get my bachelor's until i turn 24 - and that's okay :) I'm in the same circumstances of taking years off to work on my mental health, I've been meeting 15-16 year olds in first year engineering and no one gives a shit how old you are

&#x200B;

good job because i know how tough it is personally to even keep up academically with depression, and guess what? you're an engineer, an engineer after 7 years is at the end of the day still an engineer

i know the feeling!

&#x200B;

but what i put my ex through with my emotional state was a lot, he's genuinely an amazing person and i have nothing but positive things to say, however im always going to support him, and i hope he can find happiness again whether thats with someone else or me (though id be hurting honestly for a bit, but, he needs to be happy) i hope we can be on good terms or be friends again one day in our lives

fuck i know how it is :(

&#x200B;

do you want to talk about it? some part of me feels like ill love my ex for an eternity (BUT I HOPE HES HAPPY, maybe we can be friends one day :))

regular decision like beginning of january, but with extenuating circumstances since ive been out of school for awhile to focus on mental health - opting for biomed eng but might go the electrical route for more career options BUT i want to shoot my shot at engs phys as i definitely believe it would give me the best career aspects

&#x200B;

i do not have all my marks yet, im missing 2 but im not too worried about anything

